@meta
id: 14-04
title: Drill — the whole-file rename
chapter: 14
type: drill
skills: sub-range, sub-basic
par: 22
minutes: 4
reps: 8
vscode: Ctrl-H, Replace All
open: queue.config.ts

@brief
Eight times: the refunds queue has moved from `v1` to `v2`, and this
config names it on six lines. Change all six with one command and save.

You are drilling the shape `:%s/…/…/g` until the `%` and the `g` arrive
without thought. They are the two characters people leave out.

@keys
| `:%s/old/new/g` `Enter` | every match on every line |

@hints
The range goes between the colon and the `s`. The flag goes after the
last slash.
--
`:%s/v1/v2/g` and Enter. Nothing else in the file contains `v1`, so the
pattern can be that short.

@solution
    :%s/v1/v2/g<Enter>  :wq<Enter>

Sixteen keystrokes. A pattern this short is only safe because you
looked at the file and saw that `v1` appears nowhere else. On a real
file you would write `refunds\.v1` and pay eight more keystrokes for
the certainty. Deciding how much pattern to write, for the file in
front of you, is the habit; the drill is for the shape around it.

@start queue.config.ts
export const QUEUES = {
  refunds: 'payments.refunds.v1',
  refundsDead: 'payments.refunds.v1.dead',
  refundsRetry: 'payments.refunds.v1.retry',
};

export const BINDINGS = [
  { exchange: 'payments', routingKey: 'refund.created', queue: 'payments.refunds.v1' },
  { exchange: 'payments', routingKey: 'refund.failed', queue: 'payments.refunds.v1.retry' },
  { exchange: 'payments', routingKey: 'refund.dead', queue: 'payments.refunds.v1.dead' },
];

@expected queue.config.ts
export const QUEUES = {
  refunds: 'payments.refunds.v2',
  refundsDead: 'payments.refunds.v2.dead',
  refundsRetry: 'payments.refunds.v2.retry',
};

export const BINDINGS = [
  { exchange: 'payments', routingKey: 'refund.created', queue: 'payments.refunds.v2' },
  { exchange: 'payments', routingKey: 'refund.failed', queue: 'payments.refunds.v2.retry' },
  { exchange: 'payments', routingKey: 'refund.dead', queue: 'payments.refunds.v2.dead' },
];
